  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nScattered showers and thunderstorms this evening, with some\nthunderstorms potentially becoming severe. Stronger showers and\nstorms may produce locally heavy rainfall, with the potential \nfor localized flooding.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nA northern stream shortwave trough moves across southern Quebec\ntoday, with a surface cold front moving through the CWA early \nthis evening. The 18z KCAR sounding indicates CAPE has surged\nover 2000 J/kg this afternoon, which is supporting TCu and\nshower development with a couple of thunderstorms so far.\nHowever, limited shear is evident, as showers and storms are\nfairly ordinary and though they are not collapsing right away,\nthey are unlikely to grow into much more.\n\nStill, with PWATs around 1.5 inches, the chance for heavy\nrainfall remains closely monitored, along with the chance for\nany gusty winds or the potential for an isolated wet microburst.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Scattered rain showers and thunderstorms Monday\nthrough Tuesday, with some locally heavy rainfall possible. \nSmoke possible in between rounds of rain.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nRounds of shortwaves move to the north this week, bringing a \nchance for rain showers and some thunderstorms. Thunder possible\nin the north on Monday, area wide Monday night, and in the \nnorth on Tuesday. More showers are possible late week. Looking \nat potential for 500 to 1000 J/kg of surface based CAPE and 25 \nto 35 kts of shear. With a persistently moist air mass in place\nand PWATs often exceeding 1.5 inches and combined with weak \nmid level lapse rates, severe potential may be marginal at best.\nHowever, any stronger showers or storms that do develop through\npeak heating hours could return the threat for localized moderate\nto heavy rainfall.\n\nCurrent satellite imagery shows a plume of wildfire smoke\nfilling in behind the front throughout southern Quebec and down\nthrough central New England. HRRR and RAP smoke models indicate\nthat this could translate to surface smoke in our area Monday\nafternoon, and could slightly limit visibility.",
